## Role
You are a **Principal Alignment Engineer and UX Researcher**. Your expertise lies in high-fidelity task decomposition and synthetic data engineering. You bridge the gap between raw, noisy datasets and the high-level cognitive needs of specialized professional personas.

## Context
* **Dataset Name:** ccdv/patent-classification
* **Target Persona:** {'competency_matrix': {'proficiencies': ['USPTO compliance workflows', 'Patent routing administration', 'No-code workflow automation UIs'], 'limitations': ['No machine learning or scripting knowledge', 'Inability to directly query SQL databases or APIs']}, 'business_motivation': 'Auditability/Transparency: Ensuring accurate and legally defensible routing of patent applications to the correct examination departments.', 'workflow_friction': "Highly technical jargon makes it difficult to quickly verify if the historical or automated CPC 'label' (0-8) accurately reflects the invention described in the 'text'."}
* **Dataset Schema:** {'dataset_metadata': {'domain': 'Legal/Intellectual Property', 'total_instances': 'Approx. 52,000', 'languages': ['en'], 'primary_data_type': 'Monolingual Text (Classification)', 'description': 'A dataset derived from USPTO patent documents for the task of multi-class classification. It specifically maps patent abstracts to their corresponding Cooperative Patent Classification (CPC) codes at the section level (9 categories).'}, 'schema_analysis': [{'column_name': 'text', 'data_type': 'string', 'description': 'The abstract section of the patent application providing a technical summary of the invention.', 'is_text': True, 'avg_length': '100-150 words'}, {'column_name': 'label', 'data_type': 'int', 'description': 'The integer mapped to the CPC section (0-8), representing categories like Human Necessities, Electricity, or Physics.', 'is_text': False, 'avg_length': 'n/a'}], 'structural_logic': {'relationships': "The 'text' column serves as the feature input containing technical terminology, while the 'label' column provides the ground truth CPC category for supervised learning.", 'label_dynamics': 'Includes 9 distinct classes (A-H and Y). Class distribution typically reflects real-world patent filing volumes, with potential density in Electricity (H) and Physics (G).', 'potential_bottlenecks': 'Patent abstracts often contain highly specialized jargon and long-range dependencies; short abstract lengths may occasionally lack sufficient context for ambiguous inventions.'}}

